Translate Metal libraries for the iOS Simulator too.

translate_metallib.py targets air64-apple-ios only, which a device's Metal builds. The
iOS Simulator's Metal needs AIR for the simulator (air64-apple-iosN-simulator): handed
desktop AIR, or iOS AIR, it loads the library but its command buffers fail with an
internal error and the next ones never complete (seen with Brighter Shores, whose first
frame then never finishes). translate() takes simulator=True, and the command line
--simulator, to target the simulator with the same AIR revisions. Upstream candidate:
brand-free; device translations are unchanged.

